<div class="terms-page container py-5">
  <div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 800px;">

    <header class="mb-5 text-center">
      <h1 class="terms-title font-orbitron text-haitian-blue mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-muted lead mx-auto" style="max-width: 640px;">
        Your privacy matters. This policy explains how BonID collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal data.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="terms-content">

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">1. Who We Are</h3>
        <p>
          BonID is a biometric digital identity platform operated by <strong>Verifyem</strong>.
          We provide identity verification services for Haitian citizens, diaspora members, visitors,
          and partner organizations. This Privacy Policy applies to all users of BonID's website,
          applications, and APIs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">2. Data We Collect</h3>
        <p>We collect the following categories of personal data:</p>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4 mb-2">a) Identity Information</h5>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Full name, date of birth, sex, place of birth</li>
          <li>National ID number (NIF/CIN) or passport number</li>
          <li>Address and commune of residence</li>
          <li>Nationality and country of residence (for diaspora users)</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4 mb-2">b) Biometric Data</h5>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Facial photograph from your identity document</li>
          <li>Live selfie captured during liveness detection</li>
          <li>Facial comparison scores and liveness confidence results</li>
          <li>Digital signature captured during verification</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4 mb-2">c) Account & Contact Data</h5>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Email address and phone number</li>
          <li>Login credentials (password is encrypted and never stored in plain text)</li>
          <li>Communication preferences</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4 mb-2">d) Technical & Usage Data</h5>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>IP address, browser type, device information</li>
          <li>Pages visited, timestamps, and session duration</li>
          <li>QR code scan logs (who scanned, when, and where)</li>
        </ul>

        <h5 class="fw-semibold mt-4 mb-2">e) Waitlist & Partner Data</h5>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Email, commune, signup type, sector, and organization name</li>
          <li>Invite codes and referral codes</li>
          <li>PNH rank, unit type, and unit name (for law enforcement signups)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">3. How We Use Your Data</h3>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li><strong>Identity verification:</strong> To confirm you are who you claim to be using document validation, facial comparison, and liveness detection.</li>
          <li><strong>Account management:</strong> To create, maintain, and secure your BonID account.</li>
          <li><strong>Partner verifications:</strong> To respond to authorized verification requests from approved partner organizations with your consent.</li>
          <li><strong>Security & fraud prevention:</strong> To detect, prevent, and investigate fraudulent or unauthorized activity.</li>
          <li><strong>Communication:</strong> To send account notifications, verification results, and platform updates.</li>
          <li><strong>Platform improvement:</strong> To analyze usage patterns and improve our services (using anonymized/aggregated data only).</li>
          <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> To comply with applicable Haitian and international laws and regulations.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">4. Biometric Data Processing</h3>
        <p>
          BonID uses <strong>AWS Rekognition</strong> for facial liveness detection and face comparison.
          We take biometric data seriously:
        </p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>Liveness selfies are used solely for verification and face comparison — they are not used for surveillance.</li>
          <li>Facial comparison scores are stored for audit purposes. Raw biometric templates are not stored by BonID.</li>
          <li>AWS processes biometric data in accordance with their data processing agreements and does not retain face data after processing.</li>
          <li>You can request deletion of your biometric data at any time by contacting us.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">5. Data Sharing</h3>
        <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data. We share data only in these cases:</p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li><strong>Approved partners:</strong> When a partner organization makes an authorized verification request, they receive only the verification result (verified/not verified) and limited identity data — never your full documents or biometrics.</li>
          <li><strong>Law enforcement:</strong> If required by valid Haitian legal process (court order, warrant, or lawful subpoena).</li>
          <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> AWS (hosting, biometrics), email delivery services — all bound by data processing agreements.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal obligations:</strong> When required to comply with applicable law or protect the rights and safety of our users.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">6. Data Storage & Security</h3>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li>All data is encrypted in transit (TLS 1.2+) and at rest (AES-256).</li>
          <li>Identity documents and biometric data are stored in secure AWS S3 buckets with strict access controls.</li>
          <li>Passwords are hashed using bcrypt — we never store plain-text passwords.</li>
          <li>API access requires authenticated keys and bearer tokens with rate limiting.</li>
          <li>All verification requests and QR scans are logged for audit and abuse detection.</li>
          <li>We conduct regular security reviews and follow industry best practices.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">7. Data Retention</h3>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li><strong>Active accounts:</strong> Data is retained for as long as your account is active.</li>
          <li><strong>Deleted accounts:</strong> Personal data is deleted within 30 days of account deletion request. Anonymized audit logs may be retained for legal compliance.</li>
          <li><strong>Waitlist signups:</strong> Data is retained until you register an account or request removal.</li>
          <li><strong>Verification logs:</strong> Scan and verification records are retained for 5 years for security and legal purposes.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">8. Your Rights</h3>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="terms-list">
          <li><strong>Access:</strong> Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
          <li><strong>Correction:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
          <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> Request deletion of your personal data and biometric records.</li>
          <li><strong>Revocation:</strong> Revoke your BonID QR code at any time, invalidating all previous codes.</li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw consent:</strong> Withdraw consent for partner verifications at any time through your account settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Portability:</strong> Request your data in a machine-readable format.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:support@verifyem.ht" class="text-primary fw-semibold">support@verifyem.ht</a>.
          We will respond within 30 days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">9. Children's Privacy</h3>
        <p>
          BonID is not intended for use by individuals under 18 years of age.
          We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.
          If we discover that a minor has created an account, we will promptly delete it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">10. Cookies</h3>
        <p>
          BonID uses cookies to ensure the platform works securely. For full details on cookies,
          please see our <a href="#" onclick="document.querySelector('[data-controller=cookie-consent]').classList.remove('d-none'); return false;" class="text-primary fw-semibold">Cookie Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">11. International Data Transfers</h3>
        <p>
          Your data may be processed on servers located outside Haiti (including the United States)
          through our cloud infrastructure provider (AWS). All transfers are protected by encryption
          and data processing agreements that ensure your data receives the same level of protection.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-5">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">12. Changes to This Policy</h3>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make material changes,
          we will notify you via email or through the platform. The "Last updated" date at the bottom
          of this page indicates when the policy was last revised.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-4">
        <h3 class="terms-heading">13. Contact Us</h3>
        <p>For privacy-related questions or data requests:</p>
